    "details": {
      "alignment": "Unaligned",
      "type": {
        "value": "construct",
        "subtype": "Fury-Bot"
      },
      "cr": 4,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Fawful's Forces packet sheet — Boom-Crawler.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-forge-packets.py</code> from the NPC Forge roster <code>data/forge/fawfuls-forces.json</code> (entry <code>boom-crawler</code>): Large construct (Fury-Bot), Unaligned; CR 4 (proficiency +2, to hit +6 with STR); AC 14 (cast-iron barrel housing), hit points 68 (8d10+24), speed 30 ft., climb 20 ft.. A GM scene kit for the Fawful's Forces article's present (1040 BF), not a filed event; the faction article stays the authority.</p><p>A piece of the castle's main cannon that learned to walk. The Boom-Crawler is what the Fury Meter means when the article says the whole castle becomes a weapon — not one gun on the roof but a dozen smaller ones on legs, crawling along the galleries and firing down into the courtyards. Each is crewed by nothing; the fuse lights itself.</p><p>Treat it as a siege encounter. The shell is the threat, the recharge is the rhythm, and the vent after each shot is the opening: it is slow, hot and easy to hit for a round. A brave hand on the muzzle can jam the barrel and let the crawler blow its own breech. Keep the party spread so one shell never catches three.</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> artillery · <strong>tier:</strong> Fury-Bot · <strong>folder:</strong> Fawful's Furious Freaks / Machines of Fury.</p><h3>Art</h3><p>Token plate <code>portraits/fawfuls-forces/boom-crawler.png</code> — NPC Forge render, seed 410006, cut from a flat #FF00FF field. Prompt: <q>Clean cel-shaded cartoon character art in the style of Mario &amp; Luigi RPG concept art, bold dark outlines, flat colours, simple shading. A large cannon-shaped robot: a big dark green iron cannon barrel body with brass bands and rivets, a single round yellow eye on the breech, six jointed brass spider legs, a lit sparking fuse on top, small puffs of smoke. Full body, whole figure visible, three-quarter view, centred, isolated on a plain flat solid magenta background (#FF00FF), no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no border.</q></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
